Falsifies `capability::split_never_widens_rights`.

The defect: `Cap::mint_child` unions `GRANT` into the child's rights instead of
inheriting the parent's. This is the exact escape the doc comment on `mint_child`
says routing `MemoryRegion::SPLIT` through it exists to close: a spend-only
(GRANT-less) untyped splitting itself a GRANT-bearing child, and so manufacturing
the delegation right its own capability was denied. The `derive` proof does not
reach a mint, so nothing else in this crate would notice.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(child.rights, parent.rights, "an inheriting mint
changed the child's rights")`, on any parent whose rights lack `GRANT`. Measured:
exactly one check fails, `core::panicking::assert_failed_inner`, which is that
`assert_eq!`. The weaker `assert!(child.rights.is_subset_of(parent.rights))` on the
next line is a second statement of the same break, but it is never reached, because
the equality panics first.

diff --git a/crates/capability/src/lib.rs b/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
index dcd2cbb5..31a11508 100644
--- a/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
@@ -167,7 +167,7 @@ impl<O> Cap<O> {
     pub fn mint_child(&self, object: O) -> Capability<O> {
         Capability {
             object,
-            rights: self.rights,
+            rights: self.rights.union(Rights::GRANT),
         }
     }
 }
